          "path": "_m/u/1/0/k/priestfield-stadium-wp/priestfield-stadium-gillingham-1.jpg",
          "filename": "Priestfield Stadium, Gillingham Football Club - geograph.org.uk - 649957.jpg",
          "caption": "Priestfield Stadium, Gillingham Football Club This is the Gordon Road entrance. In many ways this is not an ideal place for a stadium -- it is in the middle of a densely populated residential area. There are no off street parking facilities for residents, let alone visitors. If the stadium relocated and the land was sold for housing it would fetch a lot of money. Relocating is easier said than done, though.",
          "alt": "Priestfield Stadium, Gillingham Football Club This is the Gordon Road entrance. In many ways this is not an ideal place for a stadium -- it is in the middle of a densely populated residential area. There are no off street parking facilities for residents, let alone visitors. If the stadium relocated and the land was sold for housing it would fetch a lot of money. Relocating is easier said than done, though.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 480,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Danny Robinson",
